    "title": "Carbondale man sentenced to 11 years on gun charge - NewsBreak",
    "text": "By Elizabeth Crider ,\n19 hours ago JACKSON COUNTY, Ill. — Galon Mack, 58, of Carbondale, was sentenced to 11 years in the Illinois Department of Corrections for unlawful possession of a weapon. According to a release from the Jackson County State's Attorney, the state presented evidence at trial tending to show that Mack was intoxicated during a traffic stop on Sept. 17, 2025. Officers removed Mack from the vehicle and observed drug paraphernalia in plain view. When law enforcement conducted a probable cause search, a firearm was located in the vehicle's trunk. Read full article\n1",
    "summary": "10 hours ago JACKSON COUNTY, Ill. — Galon Mack, 58, of Carbondale, was sentenced to 11 years in the Illinois Department of Corrections for unlawful possession of a weapon. According to a release from the Jackson County State's Attorney, the state presented evidence at trial tending to show that Mack was intoxicated during a traffic stop on Sept. 17, 2025. Officers removed Mack from the vehicle and observed drug paraphernalia in plain view. When law enforcement conducted a probable cause search, a firearm was located in the vehicle's trunk. Read full article",
